-- title:
--   Local structure of H⁰ at a point of fibre rank ≤ 1
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $G$ be a two-term complex over $R$ in the sense of the project: a pair of $R$-modules $C^0$, $C^1$, each finite and free, together with an $R$-linear map $d : C^0 \to C^1$ (here the modules are taken in the same universe as $R$). Let $\mathfrak p$ be a point of the prime spectrum of $R$, and assume that the fibre rank $\dim_{\kappa(\mathfrak p)} \ker\bigl(d \otimes_R \kappa(\mathfrak p)\bigr)$ of $G$ at $\mathfrak p$, where $\kappa(\mathfrak p)$ is the residue field of $\mathfrak p$, is at most $1$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an element $h \in R$ and an ideal $J \subseteq R$ such that $h \notin \mathfrak p$ and such that for every commutative $R$-algebra $B$ (in the same universe) in which the image of $h$ under the structure map $R \to B$ is a unit, the $B$-module `G.H0 B` attached to $G$ by base change to $B$ — the degree-zero cohomology of the base-changed complex — is isomorphic, as a $B$-module, to the annihilator in $B$ of the ideal $JB$ generated by the image of $J$; the isomorphism is asserted only in the form that the type of such $B$-linear equivalences is nonempty.
--
--   This is the affine-algebraic core of the local structure of the kernel functor $B \mapsto H^0(G \otimes_R B)$ of a two-term complex of finite free modules near a point where the fibre has kernel of dimension at most one: over a basic open neighbourhood of $\mathfrak p$ the functor is represented as the annihilator of a single ideal $J$, which cuts out the locus where the kernel is as large as possible. It is used in the proof that the locus where an invertible module on a family of schemes becomes trivial is cut out by an ideal, in the form of a criterion stating that the relevant ideal has trivial extension.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CoherentBaseChange_TwoTermComplex_exists_nonempty_H0_linearEquiv_annihilator_of_fibreH0_le_one.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicGeometry_CoherentBaseChange

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
